Fillets: patch 0980's guide built from a stretch of the edge before its
start (after its end) only where the spine turns at that edge's end
(mitcad#343).

The case: a bar's outline rounded with 0.3 on both sides (patch 0961's
case), each side's chain of tangent edges starting at the vertex where its
blend vanishes; the walked piece of the chain's first edge ends 0.018 past
the next edge's start, where that edge's analytic piece starts. 0980
builds such a guide, which ends a hair past the start of an edge, from a
stretch of that edge as well, so that a turn of the spine at the vertex is
not made within the hair (a fin's top edges kinked by a degree and a half,
0980's case). Here the edges go on tangentially (their tangents 2e-6 rad
apart at the vertex): there is no turn to make, and the guide, an
approximation across the vertex, passed its end 1e-5 mm and 5e-4 rad off
the spine's point and tangent, where the analytic piece's section is; the
walk's first step from that section failed, on all four chains, on the
replayed and on the stored body. Without the stretch the guide's end is the
spine's (within 1e-6 mm and 1e-6 rad) and the walk builds as before 0980.

ChFi3d_PerformElSpine now takes the stretch only where the spine's
tangents just before and after that edge's end vertex lie more than a
thousandth of a radian apart.

On the design's body before the item: valid, the stored body's 174 faces,
the change of volume -2.2689 mm3 on the stored body (as with 0961 alone);
the fin's top edges of 0980's case keep their stretch and build as before.

Upstream: new.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
index bfc749d9..865a08f3 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx
@@ -7064,7 +7064,22 @@ Standard_EXPORT void ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(occ::handle<ChFiDS_ElSpine>& HES,
   // beyond its start. The walk's sections there turn with it, the first
   // section's reframing, which looks a little before the start, finds no
   // section on its arcs, and the walk fails. The stretch is the guide's
-  // run on along the spine, where the analytic piece is.
+  // run on along the spine, where the analytic piece is. Only where the
+  // spine turns at that edge's end (by more than a thousandth of a radian):
+  // where its edges go on tangentially there is no turn to make, and the
+  // guide built with the stretch, an approximation across the vertex,
+  // passed its end 1e-5 mm and 5e-4 rad off the spine's point and tangent,
+  // where the analytic piece's section is; the walk's first step from that
+  // section failed (a rounding along a chain of tangent edges whose walked
+  // piece ends a hair past the next edge's start, mitcad#343).
+  const auto turnsAt = [&Spine](const double W) {
+    const double aStep = 1.e-5;
+    gp_Pnt       aP;
+    gp_Vec       aT0, aT1;
+    Spine->D1(W - aStep, aP, aT0);
+    Spine->D1(W + aStep, aP, aT1);
+    return aT0.Magnitude() > gp::Resolution() && aT1.Magnitude() > gp::Resolution() && aT0.Angle(aT1) > 1.e-3;
+  };
   double aPreDeb = 0., aPreFin = 0.;
   if (!periodic && !ES.IsPeriodic() && IL > IF)
   {
@@ -7073,7 +7088,7 @@ Standard_EXPORT void ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(occ::handle<ChFiDS_ElSpine>& HES,
     {
       const double aPiece = Spine->LastParameter(IF) - WF;
       const double aRoom  = WF - Spine->FirstParameter(IF);
-      if (aPiece < 0.01 * aGuideLength && aRoom > 10. * aPiece)
+      if (aPiece < 0.01 * aGuideLength && aRoom > 10. * aPiece && turnsAt(Spine->LastParameter(IF)))
       {
         aPreDeb = std::min(0.03 * aGuideLength, aRoom);
       }
@@ -7082,7 +7097,7 @@ Standard_EXPORT void ChFi3d_PerformElSpine(occ::handle<ChFiDS_ElSpine>& HES,
     {
       const double aPiece = WL - Spine->FirstParameter(IL);
       const double aRoom  = Spine->LastParameter(IL) - WL;
-      if (aPiece < 0.01 * aGuideLength && aRoom > 10. * aPiece)
+      if (aPiece < 0.01 * aGuideLength && aRoom > 10. * aPiece && turnsAt(Spine->FirstParameter(IL)))
       {
         aPreFin = std::min(0.03 * aGuideLength, aRoom);
       }
